.TH PKGCONFU 1 "2026-09-09" "pkgconfu 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pkgconfu \- report metadata, compile and link flags for installed libraries
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pkgconfu
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
\fIPACKAGE\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pkgconfu
reads pkg-config metadata files (\fB.pc\fR) and prints the compiler and linker
flags an application needs in order to use the named libraries. It resolves
\fBRequires\fR and \fBRequires.private\fR dependencies and performs variable
substitution.
.PP
This is a partial reimplementation of pkg-config. It covers the common subset
of the interface. Dependency traversal and flag deduplication follow pkgconf;
output matches the system pkg-config for most package files but a few
deduplication corner cases still differ.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the pkgconfu version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-modversion
Print the version of each package.
.TP
.B \-\-exists
Exit with status 0 if every package (and its dependencies) is found and
satisfies the requested version constraints, non-zero otherwise. Produces no
output unless \fB\-\-print\-errors\fR is given.
.TP
.B \-\-cflags
Print compile flags.
.TP
.B \-\-cflags\-only\-I
Print only \fB\-I\fR flags.
.TP
.B \-\-cflags\-only\-other
Print compile flags other than \fB\-I\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-libs
Print link flags.
.TP
.B \-\-libs\-only\-l
Print only \fB\-l\fR flags.
.TP
.B \-\-libs\-only\-L
Print only \fB\-L\fR flags.
.TP
.B \-\-libs\-only\-other
Print link flags other than \fB\-l\fR and \fB\-L\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-static
Include \fBLibs.private\fR and \fBRequires.private\fR in link output, for
static linking.
.TP
.BI \-\-variable= NAME
Print the value of variable \fINAME\fR defined in the package file.
.TP
.BI \-\-define\-variable= NAME=VALUE
Set variable \fINAME\fR to \fIVALUE\fR before parsing package files.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-variables
List the variables defined in each package file.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-requires
List the \fBRequires\fR entries of each package.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-requires\-private
List the \fBRequires.private\fR entries of each package.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-provides
Print what each package provides, as \fBname = version\fR lines.
.TP
.B \-\-validate
Check each package file for missing required fields and undefined variables.
Produces no output on success.
.TP
.B \-\-path
Print the filesystem path of each named package file, one per line.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-all
List every package found in the search path.
.TP
.BI \-\-with\-path= DIR
Prepend \fIDIR\fR to the package search path. May be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-\-maximum\-traverse\-depth= N
Limit dependency recursion to \fIN\fR levels. A value of 1 restricts output to
the named packages only.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-system\-cflags
Do not strip \fB\-I/usr/include\fR from compile flags.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-system\-libs
Do not strip \fB\-L/usr/lib\fR and \fB\-L/usr/lib64\fR from link flags.
.TP
.B \-\-define\-prefix
Redefine the \fBprefix\fR variable of each package to the directory two levels
above the \fB.pc\fR file, so paths track a relocated installation.
.TP
.B \-\-dont\-define\-prefix
Do not redefine \fBprefix\fR. This is the default.
.TP
.BI \-\-prefix\-variable= NAME
Use \fINAME\fR instead of \fBprefix\fR as the variable redefined by
\fB\-\-define\-prefix\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-msvc\-syntax
Emit flags in Microsoft compiler and linker form (\fB/I\fR, \fB/libpath:\fR,
\fBname.lib\fR, \fB/D\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-atleast\-version= VERSION
Require each package to be at least \fIVERSION\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-exact\-version= VERSION
Require each package to be exactly \fIVERSION\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-version= VERSION
Require each package to be at most \fIVERSION\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-atleast\-pkgconfig\-version= VERSION
Exit 0 if the emulated pkg-config compatibility level is at least \fIVERSION\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-errors
Print errors when a package cannot be resolved.
.TP
.B \-\-silence\-errors
Suppress error output.
.TP
.B \-\-errors\-to\-stdout
Print errors to standard output instead of standard error.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH PACKAGE ARGUMENTS
A package argument is a module name, optionally followed by a version
comparison operator (\fB<\fR, \fB<=\fR, \fB=\fR, \fB!=\fR, \fB>=\fR, \fB>\fR)
and a version string, for example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pkgconfu \-\-cflags "glib\-2.0 >= 2.40"
.fi
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PKG_CONFIG_PATH
Colon-separated list of directories prepended to the search path.
.TP
.B PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR
Colon-separated list of directories that replaces the built-in default search
path.
.TP
.B PKG_CONFIG_SYSROOT_DIR
Prefix prepended to \fB\-I\fR and \fB\-L\fR paths in the output and exposed as
the \fBpc_sysrootdir\fR variable.
.TP
.B PKG_CONFIG_TOP_BUILD_DIR
Value exposed as the \fBpc_top_builddir\fR variable.
.TP
.B PKG_CONFIG_ALLOW_SYSTEM_CFLAGS
If set, do not strip \fB\-I/usr/include\fR from compile flags.
.TP
.B PKG_CONFIG_ALLOW_SYSTEM_LIBS
If set, do not strip \fB\-L/usr/lib\fR and \fB\-L/usr/lib64\fR from link flags.
.TP
.B PKG_CONFIG_SYSTEM_INCLUDE_PATH
Colon-separated list of include directories stripped from compile flags.
Defaults to \fB/usr/include\fR.
.TP
.B PKG_CONFIG_SYSTEM_LIBRARY_PATH
Colon-separated list of library directories stripped from link flags. Defaults
to \fB/usr/lib:/usr/lib64\fR.
.TP
.B PKG_CONFIG_DISABLE_UNINSTALLED
If set, ignore \fB*\-uninstalled.pc\fR files.
.SH UNINSTALLED PACKAGES
If a file named \fImodule\fB\-uninstalled.pc\fR is present in the search path it
is used in preference to \fImodule\fB.pc\fR, unless
\fBPKG_CONFIG_DISABLE_UNINSTALLED\fR is set. This supports building against a
library that has not been installed.
.SH PROVIDES
If a requested module name is not found as a file, package files are scanned for
a matching \fBProvides\fR entry.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
A package was not found, a version constraint was not satisfied, or the command
line was invalid.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkg-config (1)
